.","M6 stock 2mm PROBABLE, approximate plate-local frames; no production datum.","Body/end contacts describe authored solids and visible source order; physical uncertainties unresolved.","Camera connector frames are presentation endpoint frames derived from observation; the adopted board proxies contain no solid connector body at these frames and the interior camera marker blocks are not connectors","Slot height, seated depth and the contact normal are presentation approximations from the V40 closeups, the official text and measured source geometry; they are not a manufacturer dimension, fit or electrical claim","The FPC ribbon is a zero-solid schematic: only its connected end frame is defined. No route, length, bend, pin map or camera OEM identity is inferred (Q-09, Q-10)","Pi5 reference STEP and the Zero drawing are guidance sources read in place from the ignored vault; no vendor geometry or pixels are published","The adopted HAT proxy is a 65 x 56 mm presentation envelope. V40 step 4 and 29 panels and the SunFounder Robot HAT V4.4 render indicate a Pi-sized board (about 85 x 56 mm) with the speaker and motor connectors toward the rear end; the proxy's outline and top-feature layout are not source-faithful. Placement uses only the mounting pattern and socket, which are unaffected","Actual HAT revision stays unresolved (Q-07); socket depth is schematic and is not a seating height. The socket and header touch at one interface plane by authored dimensions only","A declared approximate-height gap between the HAT and a standoff reflects stock height differences in authored proxies, not a measured clearance","No thread engagement, torque, fit or installation sweep is claimed","The motor proxy has no mounting bores or thread detail: each screw passes through the gearbox as a declared omitted-bore proxy overlap bounded by the screw's own shank volume, not an engagement or fit","The motor's two mounting-hole positions are not modelled; the gearbox is placed from its output shaft and flange face, and screw paths are taken from the traced Plate A flange holes","Plate A flange hole positions are photo-traced approximations; the 2 mm thickness is probable, not measured","Motor wires and leads are zero-solid schematic and are not routed; no electrical, torque or retention claim","Spring washer opening roll and nut hex roll about the screw axis are deterministic presentation gauges, not measured orientations","Hook and loop tape are zero-solid abstractions: no tape geometry, thickness or exact patch size is authored, and the allocated amounts remain unresolved (Q-11)","The battery is a tutorial envelope with no safety, capacity or voltage claim; its placement belongs to the next step","No installation sweep, adhesion or fit is claimed","The adopted battery envelope is 38 mm wide while the photo-traced slotted-flange inner gap is 35 mm; the V40 panel shows the battery snug between the tabs, so the traced gap is slightly narrow. The resulting interference is declared and bounded to at most 2 mm depth on every face, not hidden","Hook and loop tape are zero-solid; the adhesion contact is the touching top face and carries no strength, fit or safety claim","The battery is an external tutorial envelope with no capacity, voltage or safety claim; its integral lead is a zero-solid schematic","The battery lead's HAT-end connector frame is not established, so the connect operation of this step stays BLOCKED until the Robot HAT battery connector has a source-backed frame","No installation sweep or fit is claimed"],"status":"BLOCKED","stepId":"PX-V40-STEP-07","track":"instructional-only","unit":"mm","variantId":"rpi-zero-2-w","zeroSolidInstanceIds":["PX-V40-INS-HOOK-002","PX-V40-INS-LOOP-002","PX-V40-INS-RIBBON-FPC-001"]}
